    title: 'What programming actually is',
    plain: 'Programming is writing down a very exact list of instructions that a computer will follow, in an order you choose. A computer has no common sense: it will not guess what you meant, fill in a missing step, or notice that a step is silly. Programming is mostly the work of breaking a human wish into tiny, unambiguous steps, then writing those steps in a language a machine can read.',
