    plain: 'The frontend is everything that runs on the user\'s device: the page, the buttons, the animations. The backend is everything that runs on a computer you control: checking passwords, applying rules, talking to the database. The frontend is untrusted — a visitor can change it — so important decisions must be checked again on the backend. Full-stack engineering means being able to work on both sides and on the conversation between them.',
